    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/cobb-salad-with-mango-and-lime-dressing",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/cobb-salad-with-mango-and-lime-dressing",
      "title": "Cobb salad with mango and lime dressing",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Cobb salad with mango and lime dressing</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/cobb-salad-with-mango-and-lime-dressing.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>Cobb salads slide easily into the OTK ethos, as they\u2019re all about using up what you have to create something playful and vibrant. Here we invite you to the Cobb salad playground, using this recipe as a baseline. Dig through your cupboards, rummage through your fridge and freezer, use what you can and what you have, and then build from there \u2013 all the while keeping the spirit of abundance and fun.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/cobb-salad-with-mango-and-lime-dressing.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-05-31T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/spicy-lamb-and-baharat-parcels",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/spicy-lamb-and-baharat-parcels",
      "title": "Spicy lamb and baharat parcels",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Spicy lamb and baharat parcels</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/spicy-lamb-and-baharat-parcels.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>Puff pastry is so lovely and buttery and it works well with this harissa-spiced lamb filling. You might, however, want to reduce the amount of harissa paste if you\u2019re not a fan of fiery food.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/spicy-lamb-and-baharat-parcels.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-05-30T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/payn-ragoun-medieval-pine-nut-and-ginger-candy",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/payn-ragoun-medieval-pine-nut-and-ginger-candy",
      "title": "Payn ragoun (medieval pine nut and ginger candy)",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Payn ragoun (medieval pine nut and ginger candy)</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/payn-ragoun-medieval-pine-nut-and-ginger-candy.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>Travelers have always loved snacks. For me, it\u2019s peanut M&Ms. For the medieval European, it might\u2019ve been something like this candy. Bringing your own food was recommended by medieval travel guides, and it needed to be things that would keep and travel well. The classic go-to was hardtack, but something much tastier is this pine nut candy. While not everyone could afford it as sugar was quite expensive, it would be a welcome treat on the road for those who could.\n\nThis candy can either be chewy, hard like a brittle, or somewhere in between based on how hot you cook the sugar. Mine was in between, and it was absolutely delicious. The pine nuts are the dominant flavor, and you get the hint of ginger at the very end. Feel free to customize this candy even further by adding different spices or nuts. Cinnamon, galangal, black pepper, almonds, and hazelnuts would all be delicious and period appropriate.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/payn-ragoun-medieval-pine-nut-and-ginger-candy.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/claypot-chicken-rice",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/claypot-chicken-rice",
      "title": "Claypot chicken rice",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Claypot chicken rice</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/claypot-chicken-rice.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>If you can, cook this dish the traditional way in a claypot. You will get to enjoy a particularly crunchy layer of rice, which will form at the base and is an important characteristic of the dish. The combination of fluffy and crunchy rice, chicken generously coated in a tasty sauce and the earthy flavour of Chinese mushrooms makes this a mouth-watering and satisfying dish.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/claypot-chicken-rice.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-05-25T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/spicy-salmon-burgers-with-sriracha-mayo-pickles",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/spicy-salmon-burgers-with-sriracha-mayo-pickles",
      "title": "Spicy salmon burgers with sriracha mayo & pickles",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Spicy salmon burgers with sriracha mayo & pickles</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/spicy-salmon-burgers-with-sriracha-mayo-pickles.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>These burgers are delicious and make a really fun meal for all ages \u2013 substitute beef burgers for these at your next barbecue. The lightly pickled crunchy veg cuts through the spiced sriracha mayo and soft brioche buns.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/spicy-salmon-burgers-with-sriracha-mayo-pickles.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-05-23T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/cajun-style-chicken-fillets",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/cajun-style-chicken-fillets",
      "title": "Cajun-style chicken fillets",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Cajun-style chicken fillets</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/cajun-style-chicken-fillets.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>A bit like a Cajun version of takeaway chicken, these are filling and could easily be augmented to make a main meal if you add the coleslaw and garlic yogurt recipes. Make sure you cut the chicken into similar-sized pieces so they all cook evenly.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/cajun-style-chicken-fillets.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-05-16T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    }
